= entry .OpenSsh   OpenSSH's two key formats: the `openssh-key-v1` container and the `authorized_keys` line
-   detail
+   detail

-       The container `ssh-keygen` has written private keys in since OpenSSH 7.8 (armored as
-       `OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY`, which `PrivateKey.pemDecodable` reads through `.privateKey`), and
-       the single line — type, base64 blob, optional comment — which `id_*.pub`,
-       `authorized_keys` and `known_hosts` hold a public key as. Both are built from the SSH
-       wire encoding (RFC 4251 §5); neither is ASN.1, so each is converted to the PKCS#8 or
-       `SubjectPublicKeyInfo` document the providers take. The key types OpenSSH names and this
-       library reads are `ssh-ed25519`, `ssh-rsa` and `ecdsa-sha2-nistp256`/`384`/`521`.
+       El contenedor en el que `ssh-keygen` escribe las claves privadas desde OpenSSH 7.8
+       (con armadura ASCIIcon armadura ASCII como `OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY`, que
+       `PrivateKey.pemDecodable` lee a través de `.privateKey`), y la línea única —tipo, blob en
+       base64, comentario opcional— en la que `id_*.pub`, `authorized_keys` y `known_hosts`
+       guardan una clave pública. Ambos se construyen sobre la codificación de transmisión de
+       SSH (RFC 4251 §5); ninguno es ASN.1, así que cada uno se convierte al documento PKCS#8 o
+       `SubjectPublicKeyInfo` que reciben los proveedores. Los tipos de clave que OpenSSH
+       nombra y que esta biblioteca lee son `ssh-ed25519`, `ssh-rsa` y
+       `ecdsa-sha2-nistp256`/`384`/`521`.

=       library reads are `ssh-ed25519`, `ssh-rsa` and `ecdsa-sha2-nistp256`/`384`/`521`.
